[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676889060","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101516#issuecomment-2676889060","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101516","id":2676889060,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fjhXk","user":{"login":"Schafknuddler","id":98185456,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdow8A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98185456?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schafknuddler","html_url":"https://github.com/Schafknuddler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schafknuddler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schafknuddler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schafknuddler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schafknuddler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schafknuddler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schafknuddler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schafknuddler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schafknuddler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schafknuddler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-23T14:25:23Z","updated_at":"2025-02-23T14:27:43Z","body":"I think the issue isnt that the gizmo is displayed wrong, but during render, not the right FOV is being used. Consider this: Since the camera has an FOV of 75°, the box is 5m away from the camera, and thus must be 2* 5m * tan(75°/2) = 7.67m in width to fit the entirety of the screen width:\n\n<img width=\"451\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4fdf492b-ca7d-45d3-93cf-4ef8b7d99b8c\" />\n<img width=\"568\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d077edcf-a37c-417e-a828-4b4c94e0c7ec\" />\n\nMeasure the angle of the gizmo in top orthographic view to convince yourself that it is correctly shown.\nMight it really be that the problem lies in the rendering process?\nI stumbled upon this while making a shader that has to compute how big the frustum is at a given distance and it always seemed off, since it showed more of the scene in camera view than it should after doing the trigonometry.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676889060/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676959169","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101516#issuecomment-2676959169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101516","id":2676959169,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fjyfB","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-23T15:59:26Z","updated_at":"2025-02-23T16:00:09Z","body":"Please [test](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/contributing/workflow/testing_pull_requests.